    "decision": "Individually review all five complete files and eleven hunks of the first experimental M3 palette change. Eight complete palette declarations replace the prior set: generated tonal values and hue keys change, neutral maps move inside each color palette, and several palette names change. The definition default changes indigo to purple, primary/secondary/tertiary strip neutral metadata, neutral comes from primary, and error strips neutral metadata. Exactly three token functions change: palette-token filtering removes both neutral roles, reference-token generation takes neutral from primary, and the explicit neutral argument disappears from the generator/caller. Whole declaration bodies, all tonal entries/nested role keys and full token-function spans are retained; no numeric/color or map equivalence is claimed. All44 source cases retain identity,41 complete callbacks are unchanged and three update exact M3 expected colors. These are experimental M3 data/definition/token contracts; the add-on imports no experimental Material Sass and keeps its independently owned M2 palettes/theme/typography and historical oracle unchanged. Do not update a legacy palette, consumer map, golden or expected CSS to these new values. This source decision is not inheritance or executed M2/M3 coexistence; native legacy M3 theming remains outside the first-stable requirement. Exact compiler/Node/RxJS/peer floors, consumer/SSR/browser gates, private command-source reconciliation and independent audit remain separate. No publication.",
    "source_conclusion_only": true,
